<urn:atm:triage:finding/AI40-TCP-UDS-RATIO-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AI40-TCP-UDS-RATIO-001" ;
  triage:title "TCP/UDS comparison ratio silently relaxed below sprint doc's 90% floor for f1/f2 profiles" ;
  triage:description "Followup pass: user decision 2026-08-01, given directly to team-lead in this session -- 'we are well over the minimum ok 1k/second w/ both. 10x over the minimum.' Absolute admission throughput on both transports (f1 UDS 15,708/s, TCP 12,439/s; f2 UDS 23,182/s, TCP 19,915/s) is ~10x the sprint's minimum admission-rate requirement regardless of the cross-transport ratio. User accepts the observed f1 (79.2%) and f2 (85.9%) TCP/UDS ratios on that basis; the strict unconditional 90% floor in the sprint doc is waived for short frames. Note: this waiver is recorded from the user's direct statement to team-lead, not from arch-ctm's separately claimed (and unverifiable) direct user quote -- team-lead flagged that claim as unconfirmed before this decision landed. scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py:901's existing comparison_ratio = 0.9 if frames_per_connection >= 8 else 0.75 logic is now confirmed correct/accepted as-is; no code change required. Sprint doc (docs/plans/phase-ai/sprint-ai-40-local-transport-benchmark.md:140-141) should still be updated to document the accepted short-frame floor explicitly rather than leaving code and doc silently diverged." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:category "acceptance-criteria-gap" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
